<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for commerce, mercantile</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Stesich.
					80
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τέχνη</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ</span>. alone, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορία</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				14e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sph.</u>
				223d
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ., τά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				842d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. δίκαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					59.5
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				7.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τοὺς ἐ. νόμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					35.3
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. συμβολαῖα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				47
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐ. Χρήματα</span> money
				<i>to be used in trade</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				49
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μνᾶ ἡ ἐ</span>. the mina
				<i>of commerce,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				22.1013.34
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορικόν, τό</span>, <i>the class of
				merchant-seamen</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1291b24
			</span></i>; <i>with an aptitude for trade</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Decl.</u>
					33.7
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ptol.
					<u>Tetr.</u>
					66
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κοί, οἱ</span>, <i>camp-traders, sutlers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>imported, foreign</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. χρήματα διεμπολᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					974
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διήγημα ἐ</span>. <i>a traveller's</i>
			tale, i. e. <i>a romance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.39.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>in mercantile fashion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.6.16
			</span></i>.</div>
